-- The twin of the guard `tests/corpus/check/bad/TryDefaultCycle.beni`,
-- written in the shape of its own program:
-- `y = x?` and then `y` and `x` in the
-- same position make `x`'s type contain itself, whichever shape `?` settles
-- on — ONE `infinite_type`, the `?` defaulted to `Result` and the cycle
-- reported, not silenced. It is reported at the parameter
-- `x`, a binder (checker-v2.md §6.3, §8.2), not at the body: the occurs
-- check runs at every binder, so the cycle is met where `x` is bound, and
-- the place is the same as the guard's.
f x =
    let
        y =
            x?
    in
    if True then
        y

    else
        x
